{
  "id": "MOD_Taintbearer",
  "name": "Taintbearer",
  "description": "Mages who let the rot in. A Taintbearer's body is a vessel for corruption: it seeds Taint in whatever it touches, takes more of it into itself as fuel, and hands every affliction it carries to whoever it points at.\n\nTaint weakens body and mind and opens its bearer to harm, and when a Tainted host dies the rot moves on to the nearest one. Taint you carry yourself feeds your spells and your stamina, at the cost of your own health and focus, until you pass it on. Pass It On, Spillover and Return to Sender move your afflictions, enemy curses included, onto enemies; Rot Through gathers a target's Taint for a turn and then breaks it open. Damage scales with [TGH] and [PSI].",
  "archetype": "Intellect",
  "iconFrom": "SKILLTREE_Cursed",
  "mirror": false,
  "attributePriorities": {
    "Toughness": 4,
    "PsiPower": 4
  },
  "starterItems": [],
